claim_id|category|proposition|classification|source_url|boundary
E01|Technical event|On 17 February 2025 Kropotkinskaya PS was attacked by UAVs and taken out of service|Operator-confirmed technical report|https://www.cpc.ru/en/press/releases/2025/pages/20250217.aspx|CPC operator reports the incident and operational status; independent perpetrator attribution is not established in this ledger
E02|Continuity|CPC reported oil transportation continuing via an emergency bypass with normal marine-terminal loading operations on 18 February|Operator-confirmed continuity of operations|https://www.cpc.ru/en/press/releases/2025/pages/20250218.aspx|Operational continuity does not establish unchanged daily throughput or absence of economic costs
E03a|2024 exposure — KMG|KMG 2024 annual report states 55.7 million tonnes of Kazakhstan oil were transported by CPC representing 81% of total oil exports in 2024|Institutional 2024 annual-report estimate — keep separate|https://ar2024.kmg.kz/en/strategic-report/management-board-chairman-statement|The report does not explain the denominator in this passage; 55.7/81% should not be numerically merged with KazTransOil's different reported totals
E03b|2024 exposure — KazTransOil|KazTransOil 2024 annual report gives 54.9 million tonnes of Kazakhstan oil exported via CPC equal to 80% of total reported Kazakhstan oil exports; export-flow table totals 68.6 million tonnes|Institutional 2024 annual-report estimate — keep separate|https://kaztransoil.kz/en/to_shareholders_and_investors/annual_reports/?doc=2617&sc=ART|The adjacent export table covers oil and gas condensate; definitions and counting/reporting boundaries behind the 0.8-million-tonne gap versus KMG remain unreconciled
E04|Prospective throughput warning|In its 18 February 2025 statement PJSC Transneft attributed to CPC experts a 1.5–2-month repair expectation and warned this may reduce oil throughput volumes from Kazakhstan by about 30%|Forecast attributed to CPC experts within Transneft shareholder statement — NOT an observed loss|https://www.cpc.ru/en/press/releases/2025/pages/20250218-1.aspx|The reference volume, exact forecast horizon and implied denominator are not given; this is not an observed 30% decline in national exports, CPC annual shipments or government revenue
E05|Restoration|CPC reported that Kropotkinskaya PS was recommissioned starting 23 May 2025|Operator-confirmed technical restoration|https://www.cpc.ru/en/press/releases/2025/pages/20250523-1.aspx|Technical restoration does not measure incident-specific production, export or fiscal losses
E06|Aggregate throughput context|CPC reported marine-terminal liftings of more than 28 million tonnes during 1 January–23 May 2025, 1.4 million tonnes above the comparable 2024 period|Operator-reported aggregate actual throughput context — NOT event-specific counter-evidence|https://www.cpc.ru/EN/press/releases/2025/Pages/20250528.aspx|Terminal liftings are aggregated across oil origins and the period spans pre-disruption and disruption; positive year-on-year totals neither prove a zero incident cost nor quantify avoided or lost volume
E07a|National realized export reduction|Claim that the February station disruption actually caused a 30% decrease in Kazakhstan's total oil exports|NOT ESTABLISHED — unsupported conversion of E04 forecast to observed national outcome||Requires comparable daily/monthly Kazakhstan-origin CPC and national export series, exact event window, definition of 30% forecast and a counterfactual; no evidence of zero loss is inferred
E07b|National fiscal and economic loss|Claim of a specific USD fiscal or national economic loss attributable to the February CPC station disruption|NOT ESTABLISHED — no sourced causal impact estimate||Requires incident-attributable volume/cost changes, oil grades and realized prices, fiscal rules, FX timing, competing causes and credible counterfactual; neither E04 nor E06 supplies them
